[misc]
magpietalkpitch=You want the short version. I flew freight for the Skywatch, the Skywatch stopped answering, and I have been sitting on bonded cargo ever since with nowhere to land. Give me a roof and a market and I will make you rich enough to regret asking.
magpietalk1=Everything in this pack has a serial number. Ask me about none of them.
magpietalk2=I do not steal from my own settlement. Write that down, it saves an argument later.
magpietalk3=It was already falling. I merely arranged where.
magpietalk4=Bring me salvage. I am the only one up here who pays properly for it.
haldatalkpitch=I kept the stores after the last of them walked out. Forty years of counting barrels for nobody. I will come, and I will bring the cellar with me - you will want what comes out of it.
haldatalk1=A cellar keeps time better than a clock. Both are patient. Only one is worth opening.
haldatalk2=Bring me the raw and I will hand you back the worked. That is the whole trade.
haldatalk3=The cats used to sit on the warm vat. I did not have the heart to move them.
haldatalk4=Everything up here tastes of storm. You learn to call that seasoning.
ossiantalkpitch=I stayed for the archive, not the order. Half of it is unreadable and the other half I have read too often. I have things in my bag from further out than this sky - and a price, which you will not like.
ossiantalk1=I have read every roster the Skywatch kept. Yours is the first new name in a long while.
ossiantalk2=What I sell did not come from here. Do not ask where it did.
ossiantalk3=The tower is not a ruin. A ruin has stopped meaning something.
ossiantalk4=Bring me bars, not ore. I have no patience left for smelting.
spiremarker=Warden's Spire
stairsmarker=Your stairway
dirnorth=north
dirnortheast=north-east
direast=east
dirsoutheast=south-east
dirsouth=south
dirsouthwest=south-west
dirwest=west
dirnorthwest=north-west
wardenintro1=Hm. Stairs. Nobody has taken the stairs in a long, long while.
wardenintro2=I am the Warden. The last one, if you keep count. I keep the light. Kept, rather. It went out with the storm.
wardenintro3=Take this windsilk. You climbed all this way; it would be rude to send you off with empty pockets.
wardenrecruit1=Here is a strange thing to ask a stranger: my order kept the sky for four hundred years, and I am the last name on its roster. A keeper without a tower is just an old man in the wind.
wardenrecruit2=Hire me. One hundred thousand coins - the Skywatch pension was generous, and I intend to spend it working. Build me a tower of my own down there, give me a bed, and I will keep YOUR light instead.
wardenrecruitconfirm=You have the coin on you, then. Say the word again and it is done - I will not take it from you unasked.
wardenrecruitwait=A hundred thousand, friend. Coin first - then you get the oldest sky-sailor in the Reach as a neighbour.
wardenrecruitdone1=Ha! Paid in full. Then it is settled: the Skywatch serves a new house now. Yours.
wardenrecruitdone2=I will take the long way down and wait by your stairway. Go on home, build me something with a view - and we will see what else is still worth finding up here.
wardenrecruitnohome=You climbed into my sky without leaving a stairway behind you? Go home, set your front door in order - then we will talk about me moving.
wardengivesbell=One more thing. Take the old bell - it opens doors that are not doors. You will know when.
wardensettlertip=Recruited above the clouds, for a fortune in coin.
wardenfarewell=The tower is quiet now. My new post suits me better.
gatenobinding=The gate hums, dormant.\nIt has nowhere to take you yet - ascend from your own stairway first.
wardenshopclosed=My shelves are dark, like everything else here. Light the beacon first.
wardencatfound1=Mrrp?
wardencattreat=The cat snatches the treat and vanishes in a puff of cloud -\nstraight to the basket in the Warden's Spire, <dist> tiles <dir> of here.
wardencatnotreat=The cat eyes you warily.\nIt clearly expects a snack.
wardencatpurr=Prrrrt.
wardencatathome=This one has moved in for good.\nIt sleeps in the basket in the Warden's Spire now.
wardencatathomebasket=This one has moved in for good.\nIts basket is at <x>, <y> - that is home now.
wardencattreatbasket=The cat snatches the treat and vanishes in a puff of cloud -\nstraight to the basket you set out at <x>, <y> in the <level>.
catbasketready=The basket is ready, and empty.\nSiggi and Peanut are still up in the Skyreach - find them and offer a Cloudpuff Treat,\nand they will move in here.
catbasketmovedin=The cats know a good basket when they see one:\n<count> cat(s) just moved in at <x>, <y>.
catbasketmoved=The newest basket wins:\n<count> cat(s) left the old one and moved into this one at <x>, <y>.
catbasketremoved=The basket is gone, so the cats went back to the basket in the Warden's Spire.\nPut another one down and they will come to it.
wardentalk1=The wind up here has no manners. You get used to it.
wardentalk2=Four hundred years the Skywatch kept this sky. Now it keeps me.
wardentalk3=Every lamp in that tower, I lit myself. Twice, some nights.
wardentalk4=The cats came with the tower. Or the tower came with the cats. Hard to say now.
wardentalk5=Down there you have weather. Up here we have moods.
wardentalk6=I have watched a great many things fall. Very few of them came back up.
wardencatsdone=Both of them. Under one roof. That is the tower closed properly - take the basket, they know it.
wardenanchordone=Metal and stone, and the old island stops wandering. It will be where you left it. That matters, later.
catmarkerblack=Siggi's lair
catmarkertabby=Peanut's lair

[quests]
swhfindspiretitle=The Warden's Call
swhfindspiredesc=Something still keeps a light burning above the clouds.
swhfindspireobj=Find the Warden's Spire - follow the flicker over the mist.
swhreturnwarden=Speak with the Sky Warden.
swhbeacontitle=Light the Beacon
swhbeacondesc=The Skywatch beacon has been dark for too long. Bring the Warden what it needs to burn again.
swhbeaconreward=2x Flickerlight Garland
swhcatstitle=The Spire Cats
swhcatsdesc=Two cats still roam the storm and the shoals. A cloud puff treat will convince them to come home.
swhcatblack=Coax the black cat home (roams the Stormveil)
swhcattabby=Coax the tabby cat home (roams the Aurora Shoals)
swhcatblackhome=Siggi is home - asleep in the basket at the Warden's Spire
swhcattabbyhome=Peanut is home - asleep in the basket at the Warden's Spire
swhcatsreward=10x Stormsteel Bar + Cat Basket + 2x Flickerlight Garland
swhanchortitle=Anchor the Island
swhanchordesc=The spire island drifts. The Warden can anchor it - with your metal and stone.
swhanchorreward=Stormsteel Vambrace + Skywatch Banner + 5x Aurora Petal
swhrecruitwardentitle=The Last Keeper
swhrecruitwardendesc=The Sky Warden would leave the Skywatch behind, for a price no small settlement could pay.
swhrecruitwardenobj=Hire the Sky Warden into your settlement (<cost> coins)

