[misc]
// --- where each settler comes from (settlement screen "acquire" tip) ---
magpiesettlertip=Found in the Skyreach, at a derelict Skywatch workshop.
haldasettlertip=Found in the Skyreach, at a derelict Skywatch workshop.
ossiansettlertip=Found in the Skyreach, at a derelict Skywatch workshop.
eveleensettlertip=Found in the Garden of Eden, beside a Knowledge Tree. She also travels to a settlement once Eden grass grows in it. Works Farming, Forestry and Fertilising.
mortimersettlertip=Found in the Aftergarden, beside a gravestone. He also travels to a settlement that has built a graveyard. Works Hauling, Crafting and Hunting.
caspernsettlertip=Found in the Aftergarden, beside a gravestone. He also travels to a settlement that has built an Aether Forge. Works Crafting and Hauling, and nothing outdoors.
eleanorsettlertip=Found in the Aftergarden, beside a gravestone. She never comes to you - you decide whether she stays. Works Husbandry.
knottsettlertip=Found in Crooked Beyond, at the Door Yard. He does not travel to a settlement on his own. Works Trading, and nothing outdoors.

// --- Eveleen ---
eveleentalkpitch=I came up the long way, looking for a garden somebody told me was still growing. I have not found it. But you have soil, and I have seeds nobody else up here will sell you.
eveleentalk1=Everything grows if you are patient and ruthless in the right order.
eveleentalk2=That patch is thirsty. No, do not water it. It is thirsty for something else.
eveleentalk3=I keep three seeds I have never planted. I would like to know what they are before I find out.
eveleentalk4=A garden is not decoration. A garden is an argument you are having with the ground.
eveleenasksplants=Bring me one of each: an Eden Berry, a Moon Melon, a Sun Grape. Prove to me it still grows.
eveleenplantsdone=So. It still grows out there. Good.

// --- Mortimer ---
mortimertalkpitch=You have dead to keep and nowhere to keep them. I have a spade, a hat, and no particular hurry. We can help each other.
mortimertalk1=A settlement without a graveyard is a settlement that has not been honest yet.
mortimertalk2=I hunt as well. Somebody has to bring things in, and I am already dressed for it.
mortimertalk3=Do not thank me. Thank me later. Much later, ideally.
mortimertalk4=Every stone I sell is blank. What you write on it is your business.

// --- Caspern ---
casperntalkpitch=I work metal that remembers. It is not a trick and it is not cheap. Build me a forge and I will show you what a bar is supposed to sound like.
casperntalk1=Cold iron forgets. This does not.
casperntalk2=No, I will not go outside. The fire is in here.
casperntalk3=Every bar I draw has somebody's patience in it. Usually mine.
casperntalk4=Bring me ore. Bring me dust. Do not bring me questions about where the dust came from.

// --- Eleanor ---
eleanortalkpitch=I do not know why I am still here. I thought I did. If you would rather I stayed, I will stay - I am good with animals, and they do not mind what I am.
eleanortalk1=I remember a kitchen. I do not remember whose.
eleanortalk2=The goats are not frightened of me. That is worth a great deal.
eleanortalk3=Do not be sad on my account. I am not sure I can be.
eleanortalk4=Sometimes I catch myself waiting. I have stopped asking for what.
eleanorneedessence=Not enough of me yet. <have> of <need>.
eleanorfarewell=Oh. Oh, so that was all it was.
eleanorpassedon=Eleanor thins out like breath on cold glass.\nWhere she stood there is a small lantern, still warm.

// --- Knott ---
knotttalkpitch=Every door in this yard is convinced it leads somewhere. I have believed them for longer than is reasonable. You look like someone who might prove one of us right.
knotttalk1=Going somewhere?
knotttalk2=A door that opens onto nothing is still a door. It just has manners.
knotttalk3=I do not sell keys to doors I have not tested. Test enough of them and you stop needing keys.
knotttalk4=Somebody has to keep asking where they lead. Might as well be me.
knottasksdoor=If you truly think one of these leads somewhere, prove it. Bring me what a door like that would need.
knottdoordone=Ha! So it does lead somewhere. Take this - you argued it out of me.

[quests]
// --- Eveleen, the Eden chain ---
swhedenreachtitle=Into the Garden
swhedenreachdesc=Green still grows somewhere above the clouds, richer than anything in the Skyreach. Someone still tends it.
swhedenreachobj=Find whoever still tends the Garden of Eden - look for a Knowledge Tree.
swhspeaktoeveleen=Speak with Eveleen.
swhedenplantstitle=A Taste of Eden
swhedenplantsdesc=Eveleen wants proof the garden is real: an Eden Berry, a Moon Melon, and a Sun Grape.
swhedenplantsreward=3x Knowledge Cutting + 10x Stormsteel Bar

// --- Eleanor ---
swheleanortitle=Why She Stayed
swheleanordesc=Something keeps Eleanor here after everyone else has gone on. She does not know why. Maybe you can help her decide what to do about it.
swheleanorobj=Speak with Eleanor. Hold Veil Essence to help her pass on, or come empty-handed to ask her to stay.
swheleanorreward=Pass on: Will-o'-Wisp Lantern + 14x Spiritsteel Bar. Stay: she joins your settlement + 14x Spiritsteel Bar.
swhspeaktoeleanor=Speak with Eleanor.

// --- Mr. Knott, the Crooked chain ---
swhcrookedarrivaltitle=A Door That Goes Somewhere
swhcrookedarrivaldesc=Doors stand in rows here, closed on nothing. Someone still believes one of them works.
swhcrookedarrivalobj=Find whoever keeps the Door Yard - look for a red door that stands alone.
swhspeaktoknott=Speak with Mr. Knott.
swhcrookeddoortitle=Convince the Door
swhcrookeddoordesc=Mr. Knott has spent longer than anyone believing one of these doors can be convinced to lead somewhere. Bring him what a door like that would need.
swhcrookeddoorreward=Zephyr Harness + 12x Stormsteel Bar + 6x Reality Shard

